[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (2.13,1.491);
\coordinate (R) at (4.428,-1.247);
\draw[->,dashed] (P)--(0,1.3) node[above] {$N$};
\draw[->,dashed] (Q)--($(Q)+(0,1.3)$) node[above] {$N$};
\draw (P)--(Q) node[midway,above left] {$80$ km};
\draw (Q)--(R) node[midway,above right] {$110$ km};
\draw[dashed] (P)--(R);
\draw ($(P)+(90:0.8)$) arc(90:35:0.8);
\node at ($(P)+(62:1.15)$) {$055^{\circ}\text{T}$};
\draw ($(Q)+(90:0.85)$) arc(90:-50:0.85);
\node at ($(Q)+(20:1.2)$) {$140^{\circ}\text{T}$};
\node[below left] at (P) {$P$};
\node[right] at (R) {$R$};
\node[above right] at (Q) {$Q$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A ship sails $80$ km from $P$ to $Q$ on a bearing of $055^{\circ}\text{T}$, then $110$ km from $Q$ to $R$ on a bearing of $140^{\circ}\text{T}$. Find the distance $PR$, correct to the nearest kilometre.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (1.756,2.093);
\coordinate (B) at (3.233,-2.264);
\draw[->,dashed] (O)--(0,1.5) node[above] {$N$};
\draw (O)--(A) node[midway,above left] {$18$ km};
\draw (O)--(B) node[midway,below right] {$26$ km};
\draw (A)--(B);
\draw ($(O)+(90:0.75)$) arc(90:50:0.75);
\node at ($(O)+(70:1.0)$) {$040^{\circ}\text{T}$};
\draw ($(O)+(90:1.2)$) arc(90:-35:1.2);
\node at ($(O)+(28:1.55)$) {$125^{\circ}\text{T}$};
\node[left] at (O) {$O$};
\node[above] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below] at (B) {$B$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
From a base $O$, a beacon $A$ is $18$ km away on a bearing of $040^{\circ}\text{T}$ and a buoy $B$ is $26$ km away on a bearing of $125^{\circ}\text{T}$. Find the area of triangle $OAB$, correct to $1$ decimal place.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (1.477,1.761);
\coordinate (C) at (4.596,-0.188);
\draw[->,dashed] (A)--(0,1.3) node[above] {$N$};
\draw[->,dashed] (B)--($(B)+(0,1.3)$) node[above] {$N$};
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,above left] {$55$ km};
\draw (B)--(C) node[midway,above right] {$88$ km};
\draw[dashed] (A)--(C);
\draw ($(A)+(90:0.8)$) arc(90:50:0.8);
\node at ($(A)+(70:1.15)$) {$040^{\circ}\text{T}$};
\draw ($(B)+(90:0.85)$) arc(90:-32:0.85);
\node at ($(B)+(29:1.2)$) {$122^{\circ}\text{T}$};
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[above right] at (B) {$B$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A ship sails $55$ km from $A$ to $B$ on a bearing of $040^{\circ}\text{T}$, then $88$ km from $B$ to $C$ on a bearing of $122^{\circ}\text{T}$. Given $AC\approx 110$ km and $\angle ACB\approx 29.7^{\circ}$, find the bearing of $A$ from $C$, correct to the nearest degree.
